    badge: "Best Overall",
    price: "$69.99",
    oldPrice: "$139.98",
    discount: "Up to 60% Off",
    image: "/images/gf-grounded.webp",
    url: GF_LINK,
    ctaLabel: "Check Price & Availability",
    /* Rewritten 10 Aug 2026 to mechanism → payoff. The previous bullets were
       accurate and sold nothing: "Anatomically wide toe box — shaped widest at
       the toes rather than tapering" states a fact and leaves the reader to
       work out why they should care. Every winning funnel in this niche leads
       the bullet with the outcome and follows with the reason. Same facts,
       same attributions, ordered so the payoff lands first. */
    pros: [
      "<strong>The squeeze stops on day one</strong> — the toe box is widest at the toes instead of tapering to a point, so toes sit where they actually fall rather than stacked on top of each other",
      "<strong>Nothing is tipping you forward any more</strong> — heel and forefoot sit at the same height, removing the forward tilt built into almost every conventional shoe you have ever owned",
      "<strong>Your foot works again instead of being splinted</strong> — the sole is thin enough to bend and grip, so the muscles that have been carried for years start taking the load back",
      "<strong>Light enough to forget you are wearing them</strong> — the maker states 60% lighter than conventional shoes, which you notice most on hard floors late in a shift",
      "<strong>Getting the size wrong costs you nothing</strong> — free size exchanges, on the one purchase where sizing is the single biggest reason people send them back",
      "<strong>Nobody can tell</strong> — these read as an ordinary trainer, not as toe shoes",
      "<strong>They go in the washing machine</strong> — which matters more than it sounds if this becomes the pair you wear every day",
      "<strong>13,427+ customers, by the maker's own count</strong> — with a 90-day window to change your mind and free exchanges if the size is wrong",
    ],
